  "explanation": "The assessment scope is limited to hypertension. The guidelines establish that a commercial driver is unfit for an unconditional licence if blood pressure is consistently >170 systolic or >100 diastolic (treated or untreated). A conditional licence may be considered only if the driver is on antihypertensive therapy with effective control over a 4-week period, has no impairing side effects, and shows no target organ damage. The nurse note explicitly states there is 'no real patient data' regarding hypertension and provides no blood pressure measurements. Consequently, neither the unconditional exclusion nor the conditional prerequisites are met or excluded based on supplied facts.","missing_information": ["blood pressure readings (systolic/diastolic)", "antihypertensive therapy status", "4-week follow-up control evidence", "side effect assessment", "target organ damage assessment"]}
